ded."},"features":{"zh":["快速的Rust CLI工具","支持自然语言任务转换","安全的POSIX命令","支持macOS","多步骤目标支持"],"ja":["高速Rust CLIツール","自然言語タスクの変換をサポート","安全なPOSIXコマンド","macOSサポート","マルチステップ目標のサポート"],"ko":["빠른 Rust CLI 도구","자연어 태스크 변환 지원","안전한 POSIX 명령","macOS 지원","다단계 목표 지원"],"es":["CLI de Rust para macOS","Modelo integrado para tareas naturales","Salida JSON solo","Comprobaciones de seguridad","Confirmación y metas multi-paso","Devcontainer incluido"],"fr":["CLI Rust pour macOS","Modèle intégré pour tâches naturelles","Sortie JSON uniquement","Vérifications de sécurité","Confirmation et objectifs multi-étapes","Devcontainer inclus"],"de":["Rust-CLI für macOS","Integriertes Modell für natürliche Aufgaben","Nur JSON-Ausgabe","Sicherheitsprüfungen","Bestätigung und Mehrschrittziele","Devcontainer enthalten"],"pt":["Transformação de tarefas de linguagem natural em comandos POSIX seguros","Suporte a vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio","Saída JSON","Verificações de segurança","Confirmação de comandos","Devcontainer incluído"],"ru":["Преобразование задач естественного языка в безопасные команды POSIX","Поддержка vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio","Вывод JSON","Проверки безопасности","Подтверждение команд","Включенный devcontainer"],"ar":["تحويل المهام الطبيعية إلى أوامر POSIX آمنة","دعم vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio","خرج JSON","فحوصات أمنية","تأكيد أوامر","حاوية تطور متضمنة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用declutter","什么是AI智能代理","declutter替代品","declutter vs 其他工具","declutter安装","declutter设置指南","Rust CLI工具","自然语言任务管理"],"ja":["declutterの使い方","AIエージェントとは","declutterの代替","declutter vs 他のツール","declutterのインストール","declutterの設定ガイド","Rust CLIツール","自然言語タスク管理"],"ko":["declutter 사용법","AI 에이전트란","declutter 대체品","declutter vs 다른 도구","declutter 설치","declutter 설정 가이드","Rust CLI 도구","자연어 태스크 관리"],"es":["herramientas de AI","CLI de Rust","tareas naturales","comandos POSIX","modelo integrado","seguridad en la línea de comandos","alternativas a Declutter","instalación de Declutter","guía de configuración de Declutter"],"fr":["outils d''IA","CLI Rust","tâches naturelles","commandes POSIX","modèle intégré","sécurité en ligne de commande","alternatives à Declutter","installation de Declutter","guide de configuration de Declutter"],"de":["KI-Tools","Rust-CLI","natürliche Aufgaben","POSIX-Befehle","integriertes Modell","Sicherheit in der Kommandozeile","Alternativen zu Declutter","Installation von Declutter","Konfigurationsanleitung für Declutter"],"pt":["como usar Declutter","o que é Declutter","ferramentas de AI","alternativas para Declutter","Declutter vs outros","instalar Declutter","guia de configuração do Declutter","usando Declutter para automação","Declutter para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать Declutter","что такое Declutter","ИИ инструменты","алтернативы для Declutter","Declutter vs другие","установить Declutter","руководство по настройке Declutter","используя Declutter для автоматизации","Declutter для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Declutter","ما هو Declutter","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديلات ل Declutter","Declutter مقابل أخرى","تثبيت Declutter","دليل إعداد Declutter","استخدام Declutter للتحكم الآلي","Declutter للمطورين"]}},"owner":"wildcard","repo":"caro","repoPath":"wildcard/caro","stars":26,"forks":2,"updatedAt":"2026-02-08T01:22:59Z","topics":["ai","cmd","command-line","devops","local-llm","posix","runbook","rust","unix"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"declutter","description":"Identify misplaced files and organize project structure following open-source best practices, while delegating refactoring to specialized skills","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Declutter Skill\n\n**Purpose**: Create a clean, welcoming project structure where every file has its proper place, following open-source conventions and the project''s established patterns.\n\n**Philosophy**: A well-organized project should produce a hand-sized, predictable tree that immediately communicates what the project does and how it''s structured. The root should be clean and inviting, not overwhelming.\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Clean Root, Clear Intent\n\nThe project root is the first","body":"# Declutter Skill\n\n**Purpose**: Create a clean, welcoming project structure where every file has its proper place, following open-source conventions and the project''s established patterns.\n\n**Philosophy**: A well-organized project should produce a hand-sized, predictable tree that immediately communicates what the project does and how it''s structured. The root should be clean and inviting, not overwhelming.\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Clean Root, Clear Intent\n\nThe project root is the first impression. It should contain only:\n- Essential entry files (README, LICENSE, main config)\n- Standard directories that communicate purpose\n- No orphaned files, experiments, or ambiguous content\n\n### 2. Correlation Preservation\n\nFiles that belong together stay together:\n- Module-related files remain in module context\n- Development stage files stay with their stage\n- App-specific files stay with their app\n- Build artifacts stay with build configuration\n\n### 3. Skill Delegation\n\nDeclutter **identifies and recommends** but does not refactor alone:\n- For code restructuring → delegate to `refactor` skill\n- For documentation moves → delegate to `technical-writer` agent\n- For build pipeline changes → delegate to `devops` skill\n- If skill doesn''t exist → recommend installation/configuration\n\n### 4. Query Before Move\n\nWhen placement is ambiguous:\n1. First, check for relevant specialized skills/agents\n2. Consult with appropriate skill for research\n3. Only ask user when no skill can help\n4. Always explain the reasoning\n\n---\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n**Trigger Phrases**:\n- \"Declutter this project\"\n- \"Organize the file structure\"\n- \"Clean up the root directory\"\n- \"This project is messy, help me organize it\"\n- \"Where should this file go?\"\n\n**Automatic Contexts**:\n- After initial project setup\n- Before open-sourcing a project\n- When onboarding feels overwhelming\n- After feature sprawl or rapid prototyping\n\n---\n\n## The Declutter Workflow\n\n```\nPhase 1: Assessment (Survey)\n   ↓\nPhase 2: Classification (Categorize)\n   ↓\nPhase 3: Research (Consult Skills)\n   ↓\nPhase 4: Proposal (Plan Moves)\n   ↓\nPhase 5: Execution (Delegate Actions)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Assessment (Survey the Landscape)\n\n**Goal**: Understand current state without judgment.\n\n### Actions:\n\n1. **Capture the current tree**:\n   ```bash\n   tree -L 2 -a --dirsfirst -I ''.git|node_modules|target|__pycache__|.venv''\n   ```\n\n2. **Identify technology stack**:\n   - Check for `package.json`, `Cargo.toml`, `pyproject.toml`, `go.mod`, etc.\n   - Note frameworks (React, Astro, Django, etc.)\n   - Identify build systems (webpack, vite, cargo, etc.)\n\n3. **Count root-level items**:\n   ```bash\n   ls -la | wc -l\n   ```\n\n   **Healthy root**: 10-20 items (dirs + essential files)\n   **Needs attention**: 20-30 items\n   **Critical**: 30+ items\n\n4. **Identify outliers**:\n   - Files that don''t match project type\n   - Duplicate or similar-named files\n   - Dated/versioned files (backup.old, file_v2.txt)\n   - Orphaned configuration files\n\n### Output:\n- [ ] Tree captured\n- [ ] Tech stack identified\n- [ ] Root item count logged\n- [ ] Outliers list created\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Classification (Categorize Everything)\n\n**Goal**: Assign each item to a category for action.\n\n### File Categories:\n\n| Category | Examples | Action |\n|----------|----------|--------|\n| **Essential Root** | README, LICENSE, main config | Keep in root |\n| **Documentation** | *.md guides, ADRs, specs | Move to `/docs` |\n| **Configuration** | dotfiles, *.config.js | Consider `/config` or keep root |\n| **Scripts** | Shell scripts, automation | Move to `/scripts` |\n| **DevOps** | CI/CD, Docker, k8s | Move to `.github/`, `/deploy` |\n| **Source Code** | Application code | Move to `/src`, `/lib`, `/app` |\n| **Tests** | Test files | Move to `/tests` or colocate |\n| **Build Artifacts** | Generated files | Add to `.gitignore` |\n| **Experiments** | POCs, spikes | Move to `/sandbox` or delete |\n| **Orphaned** | No clear purpose | Ask user or delete |\n\n### Classification Rules:\n\n**For Markdown Files**:\n```\nREADME.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, CHANGELOG.md → Root (OSS standard)\nCODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, SECURITY.md → Root (GitHub special files)\n*.md (other) → /docs\n```\n\n**For Configuration**:\n```\nSingle dotfile → Root acceptable\nMultiple similar configs → /config directory\nBuild tool config → Usually root (webpack.config.js, etc.)\nEditor config → Root (.editorconfig, .prettierrc)\n```\n\n**For Scripts**:\n```\n1-2 scripts → /scripts or root acceptable\n3+ scripts → Must move to /scripts\nShell scripts → /scripts\nBuild scripts → /scripts/build or npm scripts\n```\n\n### Output:\n- [ ] Each file/directory categorized\n- [ ] Action type assigned (keep/move/delete/ask)\n- [ ] Ambiguous items flagged for consultation\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Research (Consult Specialized Skills)\n\n**Goal**: Get expert guidance before making moves.\n\n### Skill Consultation Matrix:\n\n| Question Type | Consult |\n|--------------|---------|\n| \"Where should docs go?\" | `technical-writer` agent |\n| \"How to structure Rust project?\" | `rust-cli-architect` agent |\n| \"Best practices for this framework?\" | `Explore` agent with framework focus |\n| \"Is this safe to delete?\" | `safety-pattern-auditor` skill |\n| \"How to reorganize build pipeline?\" | `devops` skill (if exists) |\n| \"Cultural/locale files placement?\" | `multicultural-holidays` skill |\n\n### Consultation Protocol:\n\n1. **Check if skill exists**:\n   ```\n   Glob: .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md\n   ```\n\n2. **Check if agent can help**:\n   - Review Task tool agent descriptions\n   - Match to categorization need\n\n3. **If skill/agent available**:\n   ```\n   Task: [appropriate-agent]\n   Prompt: \"I''m decluttering this project and need guidance on\n   [specific question]. What''s the best practice for [specific situation]?\"\n   ```\n\n4. **If skill/agent not available**:\n   ```\n   Report to user:\n   \"I''d like to consult a [skill-type] skill for [reason], but it''s\n   not installed. Would you like to:\n   a) Configure/install the skill\n   b) Proceed with my best judgment\n   c) Skip this category for now\"\n   ```\n\n### OSS Convention Research:\n\nWhen framework-specific guidance isn''t available, research:\n- GitHub trending repos in same tech stack\n- Official framework documentation\n- Community-accepted patterns\n\nUse the `Explore` agent:\n```\nTask: Explore\nPrompt: \"Find the standard directory structure for [technology] projects.\nFocus on: root organization, docs placement, scripts location, config handling.\"\n```\n\n### Output:\n- [ ] Skills/agents consulted\n- [ ] Best practices documented\n- [ ] User decisions recorded (if any)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Proposal (Create the Move Plan)\n\n**Goal**: Present a clear, actionable reorganization plan.\n\n### Proposal Format:\n\n```markdown\n## Declutter Proposal - [Project Name]\n\n### Current State\n- Root items: 42 (Critical - needs attention)\n- Tech stack: Rust CLI with Astro website\n- Primary issues: Documentation scattered, scripts mixed\n\n### Proposed Structure\n\n```\nproject-root/\n├── .claude/                 # Claude configuration (keep)\n├── .github/                 # GitHub workflows (keep)\n├── docs/                    # Documentation (create)\n│   ├── architecture/        # ADRs and design docs\n│   ├── guides/              # User guides\n│   └── api/                 # API documentation\n├── scripts/                 # Automation (organize)\n│   ├── build/               # Build scripts\n│   ├── dev/                 # Development helpers\n│   └── release/             # Release automation\n├── src/                     # Source code (keep)\n├── tests/                   # Test files (keep)\n├── website/                 # Astro site (keep)\n├── Cargo.toml               # Main config (keep)\n├── README.md                # Entry point (keep)\n├── LICENSE                  # Legal (keep)\n└── CHANGELOG.md             # History (keep)\n```\n\n### Proposed Moves\n\n| File | From | To | Reason |\n|------|------|-----|--------|\n| ARCHITECTURE.md | / | /docs/architecture/ | Standard docs location |\n| setup.sh | / | /scripts/ | OSS convention |\n| dev-notes.md | / | /docs/guides/ | Internal documentation |\n\n### Files to Delete\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| backup.old | Obsolete backup |\n| test_experiment.rs | Superseded by /tests |\n\n### Files Requiring Decision\n| File | Options |\n|------|---------|\n| random_script.py | A) Delete B) Move to /scripts C) Keep |\n\n### Skills to Engage\n\n1. `technical-writer` - Restructure /docs hierarchy\n2. `refactor` - Update import paths after moves (NOT AVAILABLE - recommend install)\n```\n\n### Output:\n- [ ] Proposal document created\n- [ ] All moves justified\n- [ ] User decisions requested\n- [ ] Skills identified for delegation\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Execution (Delegate and Move)\n\n**Goal**: Execute the plan with proper delegation.\n\n### Execution Rules:\n\n1. **Never refactor code directly** - delegate to `refactor` skill\n2. **Never update imports alone** - delegate to appropriate skill\n3. **Document all moves** in commit message\n4. **Preserve git history** where possible (git mv)\n\n### Move Protocol:\n\n```bash\n# Always use git mv for tracked files\ngit mv old/path new/path\n\n# Create directories first\nmkdir -p new/directory\n\n# Batch related moves\ngit mv docs/*.md docs/guides/\n```\n\n### Post-Move Validation:\n\n1. **Check for broken links**:\n   ```bash\n   grep -rn \"old/path\" --include=\"*.md\" --include=\"*.rs\"\n   ```\n\n2. **Verify imports still work**:\n   ```bash\n   cargo check  # For Rust\n   npm run build  # For JS\n   ```\n\n3. **Update any absolute references**\n\n### Commit Strategy:\n\n```bash\n# Single logical commit for declutter\ngit add -A\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\nrefactor: Declutter project structure\n\nMoves:\n- ARCHITECTURE.md → docs/architecture/\n- setup.sh → scripts/\n- dev-notes.md → docs/guides/\n\nDeletes:\n- backup.old (obsolete)\n- test_experiment.rs (superseded)\n\nCreated:\n- docs/architecture/ directory\n- scripts/build/ directory\n\nConsulted: technical-writer agent, OSS conventions\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n### Output:\n- [ ] All moves executed\n- [ ] Broken references fixed\n- [ ] Commit created\n- [ ] Post-move validation passed\n\n---\n\n## Mono-Repo Strategy\n\nFor mono-repos, declutter level by level:\n\n### Level 1: Root\n- Focus on top-level organization\n- Ensure clear separation between projects\n- Shared configs at root or `/config`\n\n### Level 2: Individual Projects\n- Apply same principles to each sub-project\n- Respect sub-project conventions\n- Don''t cross-contaminate\n\n### Level 3: Scripts/DevOps\n- Centralize shared scripts\n- Per-project scripts stay in project\n- CI/CD in `.github/` or `/ci`\n\n### Mono-Repo Structure Template:\n\n```\nmonorepo/\n├── .github/               # Shared CI/CD\n├── docs/                  # Shared documentation\n├── packages/              # Sub-projects\n│   ├── app-a/\n│   │   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── tests/\n│   │   └── package.json\n│   └── app-b/\n├── scripts/               # Shared automation\n├── config/                # Shared configuration\n├── package.json           # Root workspace\n└── README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## Technology-Specific Conventions\n\n### Rust Projects\n```\nproject/\n├── src/\n│   ├── lib.rs             # Library entry\n│   └── main.rs            # Binary entry\n├── tests/                 # Integration tests\n├── benches/               # Benchmarks\n├── examples/              # Example usage\n├── Cargo.toml\n└── README.md\n```\n\n### JavaScript/Node Projects\n```\nproject/\n├── src/                   # Source code\n├── dist/                  # Build output (gitignored)\n├── tests/ or __tests__/   # Tests\n├── scripts/               # Build/dev scripts\n├── package.json\n└── README.md\n```\n\n### Python Projects\n```\nproject/\n├── src/project_name/      # Package code\n├── tests/                 # Tests\n├── docs/                  # Documentation\n├── scripts/               # Automation\n├── pyproject.toml\n└── README.md\n```\n\nSee `references/oss-conventions.md` for comprehensive patterns.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference Checklist\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  DECLUTTER CHECKLIST                                    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                         │\n│  Assessment:                                            │\n│  ☐ Tree captured (depth 2)                             │\n│  ☐ Tech stack identified                               │\n│  ☐ Root item count: _____ (target: <20)               │\n│  ☐ Outliers identified                                 │\n│                                                         │\n│  Classification:                                        │\n│  ☐ Each item categorized                               │\n│  ☐ Actions assigned (keep/move/delete/ask)            │\n│                                                         │\n│  Research:                                              │\n│  ☐ Relevant skills consulted                           │\n│  ☐ Missing skills reported                             │\n│  ☐ OSS conventions checked                             │\n│                                                         │\n│  Proposal:                                              │\n│  ☐ Target structure documented                         │\n│  ☐ Move plan created                                   │\n│  ☐ User decisions collected                            │\n│                                                         │\n│  Execution:                                             │\n│  ☐ Moves delegated to skills where needed              │\n│  ☐ git mv used for tracked files                       │\n│  ☐ Broken references fixed                             │\n│  ☐ Commit created with full context                    │\n│                                                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## What Declutter Does NOT Do\n\n- **Does not refactor code** - delegates to `refactor` skill\n- **Does not update imports** - delegates to appropriate skill\n- **Does not delete without confirmation** - always asks\n- **Does not override project conventions** - respects existing patterns\n- **Does not move without explanation** - documents all decisions\n\n---\n\n## Skill Dependencies\n\n### Required:\n- None (can run standalone with manual moves)\n\n### Recommended:\n- `refactor` - For updating imports after moves\n- `technical-writer` - For documentation restructuring\n- `Explore` agent - For OSS convention research\n\n### Optional:\n- `devops` - For pipeline reorganization\n- `validate-constitution` - For checking project rules\n\n---\n\n## Example Invocation\n\nUsing the Task tool:\n\n```\nTask: general-purpose\nPrompt: \"Run the declutter skill on this project.\n\nFollow the workflow in .claude/skills/declutter/SKILL.md:\n1. Assess the current structure\n2. Classify all files/directories\n3. Consult relevant skills for guidance\n4. Create a proposal document\n5. Present it for user approval before execution\n\nFocus on making the root clean and welcoming.\nRespect existing conventions and correlations.\nDelegate refactoring to appropriate skills.\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\nDeclutter is complete when:\n\n- ✅ Root contains ≤20 items\n- ✅ All files are in logical locations\n- ✅ Structure follows tech-stack conventions\n- ✅ Orphaned files addressed\n- ✅ Proposal approved by user\n- ✅ All moves executed or delegated\n- ✅ No broken references remain\n- ✅ Commit documents all changes\n\n---\n\n*A decluttered project is a welcoming project. Every file in its place, every place with purpose.*\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T07:39:53.386Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing automated project structure organization and open-source convention adherence.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化项目结构组织和开源约定遵守的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが自動化されたプロジェクト構造の組織化とオープンソースの規約の遵守を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"자동화된 프로젝트 구조 조직과 오픈 소스 규약 준수를 필요로 하는 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una organización automática de la estructura del proyecto y el cumplimiento de convenciones de código abierto.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une organisation automatique de la structure de projet et du respect des conventions open-source.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine automatisierte Projektstrukturorganisation und die Einhaltung von Open-Source-Konventionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de organização automática da estrutura de projetos e aderência às convenções de código aberto.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима автоматизированная организация структуры проекта и соблюдение открытых конвенций.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التطويريين الذين يحتاجون إلى تنظيم هيكل مشروع آلي وتوافق مع الاتفاقيات مفتوحة المصدر."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create a clean and welcoming project structure by organizing files according to established patterns, utilizing JSON-only output and safety checks, and supporting multi-step goals with vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio compatibility.","zh":"使代理能够通过组织文件以建立模式、使用JSONのみ输出和安全检查以及支持多步骤目标与vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio兼容性，创建干净和友好的项目结构。","ja":"エージェントが、ファイルを確立されたパターンに従って組織し、JSONのみの出力と安全性のチェックを使用し、vLLM/Ollama/LM Studioとの互換性でマルチステップ目標をサポートすることで、クリーンで歓迎的なプロジェクト構造を作成できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 파일을 확립된 패턴에 따라 조직하고 JSON만의 출력과 안전성 점검을 사용하며 vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio와의 호환성을 통해 다단계 목표를 지원함으로써 깨끗하고 환영적인 프로젝트 구조를 만들 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear una estructura de proyecto limpia y acogedora organizando archivos según patrones establecidos, utilizando una salida JSON y controles de seguridad, y admitiendo objetivos multietapa con compatibilidad con vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer une structure de projet propre et accueillante en organisant les fichiers selon des modèles établis, en utilisant une sortie JSON et des vérifications de sécurité, et en prenant en charge des objectifs multétapes avec une compatibilité avec vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, eine saubere und einladende Projektstruktur zu erstellen, indem Dateien gemäß etablierten Mustern organisiert, JSON-Ausgaben und Sicherheitsprüfungen verwendet und mehrstufige Ziele mit vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio-Kompatibilität unterstützt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar uma estrutura de projeto limpa e acolhedora, organizando arquivos de acordo com padrões estabelecidos, utilizando saída apenas em JSON e verificações de segurança, e suportando metas em várias etapas com compatibilidade vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создать чистую и приветливую структуру проекта, организуя файлы в соответствии с установленными шаблонами, используя только JSON-выход и проверки безопасности, и поддерживая многоступенчатые цели с совместимостью vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء هيكل مشروع نظيف ومرحب به من خلال تنظيم الملفات وفقًا لأنماط محددة، واستخدام الإخراج JSON فقط والتحقق من الأمان، ودعم الأهداف متعددة الخطوات مع توافق vLLM/Ollama/LM Studio."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating project initialization with a clean and predictable tree structure","Organizing files according to open-source conventions and established project patterns","Streamlining development workflows by providing a clear project intent and structure"],"zh":["自动化项目初始化以获得干净和可预测的树结构","根据开源约定和建立的项目模式组织文件","通过提供明确的项目意图和结构来简化开发工作流"],"ja":["クリーンで予測可能なツリー構造を取得するためにプロジェクトの初期化を自動化する","オープンソースの規約と確立されたプロジェクトパターンに従ってファイルを組織する","明確なプロジェクトの意図と構造を提供することで開発ワークフローを簡素化する"],"ko":["깨끗하고 예측 가능한 트리 구조를 얻기 위해 프로젝트 초기화를 자동화하는 것","오픈 소스 규약과 확립된 프로젝트 패턴에 따라 파일을 조직하는 것","명확한 프로젝트 의도와 구조를 제공함으로써 개발 워크플ロー 를 단순화하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar la inicialización del proyecto con una estructura de árbol limpia y predecible","Organizar archivos según convenciones de código abierto y patrones de proyecto establecidos","Optimizar flujos de trabajo de desarrollo proporcionando una intención y estructura de proyecto claras"],"fr":["Automatiser l''initialisation du projet avec une structure d''arbre propre et prévisible","Organiser les fichiers selon des conventions open-source et des modèles de projet établis","Optimiser les flux de travail de développement en fournissant une intention et une structure de projet claires"],"de":["Automatisieren der Projektinitialisierung mit einer sauberen und vorhersehbaren Baumstruktur","Organisieren von Dateien gemäß Open-Source-Konventionen und etablierten Projektmustern","Optimieren von Entwicklungsworkflows durch Bereitstellung einer klaren Projektabsicht und -struktur"],"pt":["Automatizar a inicialização do projeto com uma árvore de estrutura limpa e previsível","Organizar arquivos de acordo com convenções de código aberto e padrões de projeto estabelecidos","Otimizar fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento fornecendo uma intenção de projeto clara e estrutura"],"ru":["Автоматизировать инициализацию проекта с чистой и предсказуемой структурой дерева","Организовать файлы в соответствии с открытыми конвенциями и установленными шаблонами проекта","Оптимизировать рабочие процессы разработки, предоставляя четкое намерение проекта и структуру"],"ar":["توفير تشغيل آلي لبدء المشروع مع بنية شجرة نظيفة وقابلة للتوقّع","تنظيم الملفات وفقًا لاتفاقيات مفتوحة المصدر وأنماط المشروع المحددة","تسهيل سير عمل التطوير من خلال توفير نوايا مشروع واضحة وهيكل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires caro, a fast Rust CLI, for natural-language task execution","Built primarily for macOS with MLX/Metal and may have compatibility issues with other platforms","JSON-only output may limit flexibility for certain use cases"],"zh":["需要caro，一种快速的Rust CLI，用于自然语言任务执行","主要为macOS和MLX/Metal构建，可能与其他平台存在兼容性问题","JSONのみの输出可能会限制某些用例的灵活性"],"ja":["自然言語タスクの実行には、高速なRust CLIであるcaroが必要","主にmacOSとMLX/Metal用にビルドされており、他のプラットフォームでは互換性の問題が発生する可能性がある","JSONのみの出力によって、特定のユースケースの柔軟性が制限される可能性がある"],"ko":["자연어 태스크 실행을 위해 빠른 Rust CLI인 caro가 필요함","주로 macOS와 MLX/Metal을 위해 빌드되었으므로 다른 플랫폼과 호환성 문제가 발생할 수 있음","JSON만의 출력으로 인해 특정 유즈케이스의 유연성이 제한될 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere caro, una CLI de Rust rápida, para la ejecución de tareas de lenguaje natural","Construido principalmente para macOS con MLX/Metal y puede tener problemas de compatibilidad con otras plataformas","La salida JSON solo puede limitar la flexibilidad para determinados casos de uso"],"fr":["Nécessite caro, une CLI Rust rapide, pour l''exécution de tâches de langage naturel","Conçu principalement pour macOS avec MLX/Metal et peut avoir des problèmes de compatibilité avec d''autres plates-formes","La sortie JSON uniquement peut limiter la flexibilité pour certains cas d''utilisation"],"de":["Benötigt caro, eine schnelle Rust-CLI, für die Ausführung von natürlichen Sprachaufgaben","Hauptsächlich für macOS mit MLX/Metal entwickelt und kann Kompatibilitätsprobleme mit anderen Plattformen haben","Die JSON-Ausgabe allein kann die Flexibilität für bestimmte Anwendungsfälle einschränken"],"pt":["Exige caro, uma CLI Rust rápida, para execução de tarefas de linguagem natural","Construído principalmente para macOS com MLX/Metal e pode ter problemas de compatibilidade com outras plataformas","Saída apenas em JSON pode limitar a flexibilidade para determinados casos de uso"],"ru":["Требует caro, быстрого CLI Rust, для выполнения задач естественного языка","Примarily построен для macOS с MLX/Metal и может иметь проблемы совместимости с другими платформами","Только JSON-выход может ограничить гибкость для определенных случаев использования"],"ar":["يتطلب caro، واجهة سطر أوامر Rust سريعة، لتنفيذ مهام اللغة الطبيعية","تم بناؤه في الأساس لمنصة macOS مع MLX/Metal ويمكن أن يكون له مشاكل في التوافق مع منصات أخرى","الإخراج JSON فقط قد يقيد المرونة لبعض حالات الاستخدام"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3b0c1d04b2580bababcbb9d1321d163b72dc399ea3401218853072175f444104","qualityScore":70}');
